# Frontend i18n (mandatory)

FactoryMate frontend strings live in locale files, not in components. Spec: `docs/factorymate-spec.md` §8.2.

## Stack

- **next-intl** with App Router
- **MVP locale:** `en` only — `frontend/messages/en.json`
- No language switcher in v1

## Rules

1. **Never** put user-facing text directly in JSX/TSX (`"Save"`, `'Players'`, dialog titles, toast messages, `aria-label`, empty states, column headers for UI labels).
2. Use `useTranslations('namespace')` (client) or `getTranslations('namespace')` (server/RSC).
3. Add keys to `messages/en.json` in the same PR as the UI — namespace per feature (`nav`, `auth`, `players`, `power`, `settings`, `common`, …).
4. Dynamic text: `t('key', { name: value })` — not template literals in components for translatable phrases.
5. **Do translate:** UI chrome, labels, actions, errors shown to users, nav, settings forms.
6. **Do not translate via i18n:** API/game data (player names, item names, FRM status codes shown as raw data). Discord templates are §5, not frontend i18n.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<Button>Save changes</Button>
<p>No players online</p>

// ✅ GOOD
const t = useTranslations('common');
<Button>{t('save')}</Button>
<p>{t('players.noneOnline')}</p>
```

```json
// messages/en.json
{
  "common": { "save": "Save changes", "cancel": "Cancel" },
  "players": { "noneOnline": "No players online" }
}
```

## Verification

Frontend milestone DoD includes §8.2 compliance. Reviewers grep for obvious hardcoded strings in new `frontend/` files (quoted JSX text children, label props) and FAIL if user-facing text is not in `en.json`.
